# generated by ex2-c-glue/build-and-test.sh
ex2-c-glue/include/*
!ex2-c-glue/include/.gitkeep
ex2-c-glue/test_glue

# --- Exercise 3, per track ---
#
# Each track's documented first command leaves something the root .gitignore
# does not name. These are scoped to this directory rather than added at the
# root because the same filenames are tracked ON PURPOSE elsewhere in the repo
# — the same reason ex2-c-glue's header rule is scoped instead of global.

# swiftc -o ex3, the compile line main.swift documents. An executable with no
# extension, so none of the root's suffix rules (*.o, *.out, *.so …) reach it.
ex3-bindings/swift/ex3
# ...and the debug companion, if you build with -g on macOS.
ex3-bindings/swift/*.dSYM/

# `dart pub get`, the Dart track's documented first command, writes this.
# Deliberately NOT a root rule: days/*/dart/ commits its pubspec.lock, because
# a worked example should pin what it actually resolved. This scaffold is the
# opposite — the attendee runs `dart pub get` themselves, so the lock is their
# machine's output and not something to hand them.
ex3-bindings/dart/pubspec.lock

# Not listed here on purpose: the Kotlin track's JNA jar lives in
# $XDG_CACHE_HOME (scripts/fetch-jna.sh), outside the repo; .dart_tool/ and
# __pycache__/ are covered by their own root rules.
